{
 "esm": "1.3.0",
 "metadata": {
  "name": "cam_zm_evap",
  "description": "Stage-2 implementation of the CAM Zhang-McFarlane rain evaporation step zm_conv_evap_run (stage 2 of the EqESM project; instrumented cam6_4_212 fork of the SCAM ARM97_4scam run, dump window steps 18-23 and 40-48): the per-level laws of zm_conv_evap.F90:118-236 evaluated on the dumped convr state (the zm_conv_evap_run call of zm_conv_intr.F90:671-679; all dumped columns of the window are g = 1). The evaporation of each layer: the relative-humidity depression evplimit_rh = max(1 - q/qs, 0) (F90:158), the Sundqvist rate evpprec_raw = ke (1 - cldfrc) evplimit_rh sqrt(flxprec_lo) with kemask = ke (the zmconv_ke coefficient; F90:160-164), and the three upper bounds of the Fortran's min chain - the saturation limit max(0, (qs - q)/deltat) (F90:168), the falling-flux limit flxprec_lo gravit/pdel (F90:173) and the remaining-precipitation limit (prec_gen - evpvint) gravit/pdel (F90:176) - combined as evpprec = min(min(min(limit_dt, limit_flx), limit_avail), evpprec_raw) (F90:178). The snow branch runs with old_snow = .true. (F90:108): the melt split flxsntm = 0 / snowmlt = flxsnow_lo gravit/pdel where t1 > tmelt, else flxsntm = flxsnow_lo, snowmlt = 0 (F90:128-134); the snow evaporation evpsnow = evpprec work1 with work1 = min(max(0, flxsntm/flxprec_lo), 1) when flxprec_lo > 0 else 0 (F90:186-192); the net production ntprprd = rprd - evpprec (F90:198); the net snow production ntsnprd = rprd work2 - evpsnow - snowmlt with work2 = max(fsnow_conv, work1b) zeroed when snowmlt > 0 (F90:204-215); and the fluxes flxprec_hi = max(flxprec_lo + ntprprd pdel/gravit, 0), flxsnow_hi likewise (F90:219-224). The precipitation flux is the vertical integral of the net production; the coupled top-down recurrence (the evaporation at a level depends on the flux entering it, which is the integral of production-minus-evaporation above it) cannot be expressed in the CLI - it is rejected as an observed dependency cycle (esm-spec 4.9.6; the exact CLI error is quoted in README-cam-zm-evap.md) - so this component pins the per-level step with the accumulated boundary flux flxprec_lo/flxsnow_lo taken from the dump (the recurrence boundary) and the Fortran's running accumulator evpvint supplied as a derived input: evpvint(k) = sum_{j<k} (rprd(j) - ntprprd(j)) pdel(j)/gravit, reconstructed from the dumped rprd and ntprprd columns (each increment equals evpprec(j) pdel(j)/gravit of F90:195 because ntprprd = rprd - evpprec, F90:198). qs is the estblf table lookup (wv_saturation.F90:191-254, the Goff-Gratch mixed-phase table, 251 knots at T = 127.16 + (i-1) K) followed by the svp_to_qsat conversion (eps es/(p - omeps es)); the estbl table is duplicated here as a function_tables entry (extracted verbatim from the committed cam_wv_saturation.esm table) because function tables are data, not template libraries, and cannot be imported by reference (the CLI rejects template_import_not_library; the duplication is the same data as the Fortran's estbl and is cross-checked by the cam_qsat.csv dump). Levels are the CAM convention, lev 1 = model top, lev 32 = surface, exactly as dumped. The surface rates are the bottom-interface fluxes divided by density_fresh_water = 1000 kg/m3 (F90:234-236): prec_evap = flxprec_hi(32)/1000, snow_evap = flxsnow_hi(32)/1000. Tests at steps 18, 22, 40 and 48: the step-18 and step-22 columns evaporate the precipitation fully (prec_evap = 0; the roundoff guard of F90:222-224 fires at lev 31, turning a residual flux of order 1e-19 kg/m2/s to zero); across the dumped window the evpprec min chain binds the Sundqvist rate at 401 of 480 levels (0.85 of the window), the falling-flux limit at 45 levels and the remaining-precipitation limit at 34 levels, and never the deltat saturation limit; step 22 pins the Sundqvist limit binding non-degenerately in the evanesced regime (levels 23-26) and steps 40 and 48 are the active-evaporation columns (prec_evap = 4.5e-9 and 1.0e-8 m/s) where the Sundqvist rate binds at every level with flxprec_lo > 0, so their tend_q pins exercise the qs-dependent factor max(1 - q/qs, 0) of F90:158 through the table-interpolated qs.",
  "license": "MIT",
  "tags": [
   "eqesm:stage2",
   "model:convection",
   "cam:zm"
  ],
  "references": [
   {
    "citation": "CAM6.4 (cam6_4_212, Zhang-McFarlane deep convection), components/cam/src/atmos_phys/schemes/zhang_mcfarlane/zm_conv_evap.F90, subroutine zm_conv_evap_run, called from zm_conv_intr.F90:671-679."
   }
  ]
 },
 "metaparameters": {
  "PVER": {
   "type": "integer",
   "default": 32,
   "description": "Number of model levels (pver = 32 in the SCAM run; the dump's pver)."
  }
 },
