   "tests": [
    {
     "id": "s18_g1",
     "description": "Step 18, g = 1 column (cam_zm.csv step 18 rows lev 1..32 with cam_zm_scal.csv step 18; prec_convr = 4.255483e-09 m/s, ke = 5.0e-06, deltat = 1800 s): the zm_conv_evap_run chain of zm_conv_evap.F90:118-236 pinned at the first raining levels (levs 16-17), the deep-evaporation region (lev 25, where the net production ntprprd goes negative and the snow flux has vanished so ntsnprd = 0) and the bottom boundary (lev 32, the surface rates prec_evap/snow_evap = flxprec_hi(32)/1000 of F90:234-236). The precipitation evaporates completely in the column (prec_evap = 0): at lev 31 the unclamped flux flxprec_lo + ntprprd pdel/gravit is a roundoff residual of order -1e-19 kg/m2/s and the max guard of F90:222-224 pins it to 0 (the dumped flxprec_hi(31) = 0), so flxprec_hi(32) and prec_evap are 0; lev 17 pins the evaporation of the first raining layer (tend_q = evpprec > 0); lev 25 pins the net production going negative (evaporation of the downdraft-evaporated precipitation exceeds the production) with ntsnprd = 0 below the snow region (fsnow_conv = 0, work2 = 0). The evpprec min chain binds the falling-flux limit F90:173 at 9 levels and the remaining-precipitation limit F90:176 at 6 levels of this column (never the deltat limit F90:168, which does not bind on any dumped column); the Sundqvist rate F90:164 is never the active bound with flxprec_lo > 0 here (it binds only where the entering flux is zero). lev 22 is the melting level of this column (t1(22) = 274.57 K > tmelt with flxsnow_lo > 0): the melt branch of F90:128-134 fires (flxsntm = 0, snowmlt = flxsnow_lo gravit/pdel > 0), work2 is zeroed at F90:212 so ntsnprd(22) = -snowmlt (the dumped net snow production goes negative), tend_s_snwevmlt(22) = -snowmlt latice is the melt cooling, and the snow flux vanishes below the melting level (flxsnow_hi(22) = 0, so no snow reaches the surface and snow_evap = 0).",
