     "id": "s22_g1",
     "description": "Step 22, g = 1 column (cam_zm.csv step 22 rows lev 1..32 with cam_zm_scal.csv step 22; prec_convr = 2.213691e-08 m/s, ke = 5.0e-06, deltat = 1800 s): the zm_conv_evap_run chain of zm_conv_evap.F90:118-236 pinned at the first raining levels (levs 16-17), the deep-evaporation region (lev 25, where the net production ntprprd goes negative and the snow flux has vanished so ntsnprd = 0) and the bottom boundary (lev 32, the surface rates prec_evap/snow_evap = flxprec_hi(32)/1000 of F90:234-236). prec_evap = 0 (the column evaporates its precipitation; the roundoff guard of F90:222-224 fires at lev 31, flxprec_hi(31) = 0). lev 24 pins the Sundqvist limit binding NON-degenerately: at levels 23-26 of this column evpprec = evpprec_raw = ke (1 - cldfrc) max(1 - q/qs, 0) sqrt(flxprec_lo) (F90:160-164, 178) with flxprec_lo > 0, so tend_q pins the relative-humidity factor max(1 - q/qs, 0) of F90:158 through the table-interpolated qs. The min chain binds the falling-flux limit at 6 levels and the remaining-precipitation limit at 5 levels. lev 22 is the melting level of this column (t1(22) = 274.52 K > tmelt with flxsnow_lo > 0): the melt branch of F90:128-134 fires (flxsntm = 0, snowmlt = flxsnow_lo gravit/pdel > 0), work2 is zeroed at F90:212 so ntsnprd(22) = -snowmlt (the dumped net snow production goes negative), tend_s_snwevmlt(22) = -snowmlt latice is the melt cooling, and the snow flux vanishes below the melting level (flxsnow_hi(22) = 0, so no snow reaches the surface and snow_evap = 0).",
