     "description": "Step 40, g = 1 column (cam_zm.csv step 40 rows lev 1..32 with cam_zm_scal.csv step 40; prec_convr = 7.365285e-08 m/s, ke = 5.0e-06, deltat = 1800 s): the zm_conv_evap_run chain of zm_conv_evap.F90:118-236 pinned at the first raining levels (levs 16-17), the deep-evaporation region (lev 25, where the net production ntprprd goes negative and the snow flux has vanished so ntsnprd = 0) and the bottom boundary (lev 32, the surface rates prec_evap/snow_evap = flxprec_hi(32)/1000 of F90:234-236). prec_evap = 4.540434e-09 m/s, the second-window early column (steps 40-48); the evpprec min chain binds the Sundqvist rate evpprec_raw of F90:160-164 at every level with flxprec_lo > 0 (levels 17-32) - the falling-flux and remaining-precipitation limits of F90:173/176 never bind in this column - so tend_q at lev 17 pins the max(1 - q/qs, 0) factor of F90:158 through the table-interpolated qs, and tend_q at lev 30 pins the same factor deeper in the column. lev 22 is the melting level of this column (t1(22) = 274.67 K > tmelt with flxsnow_lo > 0): the melt branch of F90:128-134 fires (flxsntm = 0, snowmlt = flxsnow_lo gravit/pdel > 0), work2 is zeroed at F90:212 so ntsnprd(22) = -snowmlt (the dumped net snow production goes negative), tend_s_snwevmlt(22) = -snowmlt latice is the melt cooling, and the snow flux vanishes below the melting level (flxsnow_hi(22) = 0, so no snow reaches the surface and snow_evap = 0).",
